# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights only. Nothing else under outputs/ is ignored, deliberately.
#
# This file previously ignored outputs/**/*.csv, *.json, *.png, summary.txt,
# final_results.csv and logs/*.log as well -- i.e. every artifact the project
# exists to produce. The consequence was silent and expensive: `git add
# outputs/dpap_repl/sparsity_curve_beta0.01` reported nothing and added
# nothing, so a commit titled "Add the beta_max=0.01 sparsity curve results"
# actually contained only two log files that happened to be forced in. Months
# of headline numbers ended up existing solely as prose in HANDOFF.md, and a
# whole session was spent trying to work out where the files had gone. They
# were never there.
#
# Results files are small (CSVs, JSONs, summaries, figures) and are the entire
# evidence base for the dissertation. They belong in version control. Weights
# are large, regenerable from a config plus GPU hours, and are backed up
# outside git -- see HANDOFF.md.
#
# If you add an ignore rule here, check it does not swallow evidence.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
checkpoints/*.pt
outputs/**/*.pt
*.pth
